INT. DRIVEWAY BASKETBALL COURT - EVENING

A cracked asphalt pad under a flickering floodlight. A hoop with a ragged net. Moths whirl in the beam. A bike lies on its side near the garage.

TEO, 16, in an oversized hoodie, dribbles the ball in a slow, thoughtful rhythm. His cousin LUKA, 17, taller, leans against the garage door with his arms crossed.

LUKA
You're stalling, Teo.

TEO
I'm warming up.

LUKA
You're stalling.

TEO
I'm warming up for stalling.

Luka pushes off the door. He strides to the court and holds out his hands. Teo hesitates, then bounce-passes. Luka catches it.

LUKA
Twenty-one. Ball to the winner.

TEO
It's your ball.

LUKA
It's about to be your ball.

TEO
You're so sure?

LUKA
I'm sure you're afraid.

Teo says nothing. Luka checks the ball to him. Teo catches it, plants a foot, fakes left, goes right. Luka slides. Teo's shot sails up and drops through the net with a clean swish.

TEO
One.

LUKA
Lucky.

TEO
One.

Luka snatches the ball and dribbles up the court. He drives, bumps Teo's shoulder, and puts up a floater. It clanks off the rim. They both rush for the rebound. Their arms tangle. They both fall, and the ball bounces away into the shadows.

TEO (CONT'D)
Foul.

LUKA
It's not a foul.

TEO
You hit me.

LUKA
You hit me.

They lie there on the asphalt, breathing hard, staring at the floodlight. A moth circles above their faces. Neither moves to retrieve the ball.

LUKA (CONT'D)
Teo.

TEO
Yeah.

LUKA
Your dad called.

TEO
I know.

LUKA
He said you're not coming home.

TEO
He said what?

LUKA
That you're staying with us. Through the summer.

Teo sits up. His face closes. He pulls his hood over his head and stares at the garage door.

TEO
He didn't tell me.

LUKA
Maybe he wanted me to.

TEO
That's cold, Luka.

LUKA
He's not cold. He's scared.

TEO
Of me?

LUKA
Of whatever he's got to say.

Teo gets up. He walks to the edge of the court, stops. The ball rolls out of the dark toward his foot. He stops it with a toe, kicks it up, catches it.

TEO
(quiet)
Twenty-one.

LUKA
What?

TEO
We play to twenty-one. I'm up by one.

Luka rises. A pause. He wipes his hands on his shorts and gets into a defensive crouch.

LUKA
Then check.

Teo checks the ball. Luka taps it back. Teo spins, dribbles, and drives to the hoop. Luka slams into him, both of them tumbling again. The ball flies out of bounds, and the floodlight clicks off, and the court goes dark.

LUKA (CONT'D)
(in the dark)
Foul.

TEO
(in the dark, laughing)
It's not a foul!
